---
// A long address or query in a sentence. It may break at any character, so that the lines of the
// sentence stay full: the browser would otherwise move the whole unbreakable word to the next line
// and leave a gap. Short code in a sentence is not meant to break in the middle, so this is a
// component of its own and not a rule for all code.
---

<code class="url">
  <slot />
</code>

<style>
  .url {
    word-break: break-all;
  }
</style>
